9
00:49:41,739 --> 00:49:47,739
Nikolai Kravinoff, played by Russell Crowe.

10
00:55:13,043 --> 00:55:19,043
Kraven the Hunter is a 2024 American superhero film
featuring the character from Marvel Comics.

11
01:00:44,347 --> 01:00:50,347
It is the sixth film in Sony's Spider-Man Universe (SSU).

12
01:06:15,652 --> 01:06:21,652
Aaron Taylor-Johnson stars as Kraven, alongside Ariana DeBose, Fred
Hechinger, Alessandro Nivola, Christopher Abbott, and Russell Crowe.

13
01:11:46,956 --> 01:11:52,956
Directed by J.C.

14
01:17:18,260 --> 01:17:24,260
Chandor and written by Richard Wenk, Art Marcum and Matt Holloway, the film explores Kraven's
relationship with his father and his path to becoming the greatest hunter.

15
01:22:49,565 --> 01:22:55,565
Kraven was considered for film appearances several times before Sony Pictures became interested in a
standalone film for the character, as part of its new shared universe, in mid-2017.

16
01:28:20,869 --> 01:28:26,869
Wenk was hired in August 2018, and Chandor entered negotiations to direct in August
2020, and was confirmed in May 2021 when Taylor-Johnson was cast.

17
01:33:52,173 --> 01:33:58,173
Filming took place from late March until mid-June
in London, Iceland, and Glasgow.

18
01:39:23,478 --> 01:39:29,478
Following two years of delays, Kraven the Hunter was released in the United
States on December 13, 2024, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

19
01:44:54,782 --> 01:45:00,782
The film was a box-office failure, grossing $62 million worldwide against a
$110–130 million budget, and received negative reviews from critics.

20
01:50:26,086 --> 01:50:32,086
Following its release, Sony halted development on further SSU films.

21
01:55:57,391 --> 01:56:03,391
The film explores themes of hunter, superhero,
villain, based on comic, supervillain.

22
02:01:28,695 --> 02:01:34,695
The tone is dark and thought_provoking and intense.
